# Nextant Solution Library — Dataverse schema (v2)

This is the current, agreed model. It replaces [nextant-solution-library-dataverse-schema.md](nextant-solution-library-dataverse-schema.md) (v1) — same base idea, refined through review: `Category` and `Use Case` were dropped as unsustainable governed tag lists, and a new `Project` concept was added to separate "the reusable Solution" from "the evidence that it's been built before."

## Conventions

- **Primary key vs. primary name** — every table gets an auto-generated GUID key (e.g. `nx_solutionid`) plus a required text *primary name* column, used as its display label in lookups.
- **System columns are automatic** — `createdon`, `createdby`, `modifiedon`, `modifiedby`, `ownerid`, `statecode`/`statuscode` exist on every table without being modeled.
- **Ownership** — `Solution`, `Project`, `ProjectEvidence`, and `DemoRequest` are **user/team-owned** (row-level security, since different practices submit their own work). `SpecializationArea`, `Industry`, and `Technology` are **organization-owned** (shared reference data).
- **Native many-to-many** — every tag relationship (SA, Industry, Technology) is a native Dataverse N:N. No hand-built junction tables.
- **Governance** — `SpecializationArea` and `Industry` are governed (only the Librarian adds new values). `Technology` is open (anyone adds a value inline; the Librarian periodically merges duplicates).

